course: dictionary
lesson: 10111
title: Thirsty and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one to use. The word thirsty can mean needing a drink, but it can also describe dry land or plants, or show that you want something very much. «When you are thirsty, drink water» is about your body.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The thirsty garden needed rain» is about dry soil and plants that need water. «She was thirsty for knowledge and read every book in the library» means she wanted to learn very much. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Your body needs water every day. «Losing too much water makes you thirsty, tired, headachy and slower.» Salty food also makes you thirsty, so a meal of salty crisps can leave you wanting a drink.
fact: Thirsty is an adjective, and its comparison forms are thirstier and thirstiest.
fact: Thirsty means needing or wanting to drink.
fact: Thirsty can describe dry land or plants that need water.
fact: Thirsty for something means wanting it very much, like thirsty for knowledge.
fact: «Children need about six to eight cups of water a day, and more when it is hot or they are active.»
exercise: «When you are thirsty, drink water.» What does thirsty mean here? | Wanting a new book very much | Dry and dusty like a desert | Very, very happy | *Needing or wanting to drink
exercise: «The thirsty garden needed rain.» What does thirsty describe in this sentence? | A child who forgot a drink | The sky above the garden | *The land and plants that need water | The gardener's tools
exercise: «She was thirsty for knowledge.» What does this mean? | She was happy about her lunch | She was tired of school | She had no drink at lunch | *She wanted to learn very much
test: Why should children drink water on a hot day? | Because thirsty means tired | *Because they need more water when it is hot | Because sugary drinks are good for teeth | Because water makes them taller
test: «Drinking seawater makes a person thirstier and ill.» What does thirstier mean? | Not thirsty at all | Wetter | Less thirsty | *More thirsty
exam: Today I am ___ than yesterday, after the long run. | thirsty | thirstiest | thirstily | *thirstier
